    "result_text": "All green. The only test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`) passes, and the full build succeeds \u2014 which includes OpenAPI DTO regeneration and MapStruct/Java compilation.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, keeping each piece of logic in a focused unit:\n\n**Format logic** \u2014 new `CustomerCodeGenerator` component (`rest/assignment/`) with a single responsibility: given a last name and the current owner count, produce `SMI-0007` (upper-cased first three letters + zero-padded `count + 1`). Mirrors the existing `EmailNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer` helpers.\n\n**Counting** \u2014 added a `count()` query to `OwnerRepository` and implemented it in all three arms (Spring Data `@Query`, JPA `EntityManager`, JDBC `SELECT COUNT(*)`), then exposed it through the service facade as `ClinicService.countOwners()`. This gives a proper count query rather than loading all owners.\n\n**Orchestration** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the `POST /api/owners` handler) now assigns the code on the new owner just before saving, reusing the generator and the count \u2014 sitting alongside the existing create-time normalization/duplicate checks. The update path is untouched, so codes aren't reassigned on edit.\n\n**Persistence & contract**:\n- Added the `customerCode` field/column to the `Owner` entity (`customer_code`).\n- Added the column to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 required because the test profile runs hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`.\n- Added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (same mechanism as the existing `displayName`/`initials`).\n\nThe acceptance test confirms both the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the global sequence increments by one between successive creates.",
